# Tool Configuration System

This document outlines the system for managing and toggling MCP (Model Context Protocol) and Agent Tools within the application.

## Overview

The tool configuration system allows users to enable or disable specific tools and entire categories of tools through the application settings. This provides fine-grained control over the AI agent's capabilities.

## Key Components

### Backend (Rust - `src-tauri`)

*   **Tool Configuration Module**: Defines the core structures and logic for managing tool settings. This includes `ToolConfigManager`, `ToolCategory`, and `ToolConfig`.
    *   [src-tauri/src/agent/tools/tool_config.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools/tool_config.rs)
*   **State Management**: Integrates the `ToolConfigManager` into the global `AppState` for persistence and accessibility.
    *   [src-tauri/src/state.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/state.rs)
*   **Tauri Commands**: Exposes functionalities to the frontend for getting and setting tool configurations.
    *   [src-tauri/src/commands/tools.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/commands/tools.rs)
    *   Registered in [src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs)
*   **Tool Provider Integration**: Ensures that tool providers (e.g., `LocalToolProvider`) respect the configured settings when registering tools.
    *   [src-tauri/src/agent/implementations/tool_provider.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/implementations/tool_provider.rs)

### Frontend (TypeScript/React - `src`)

*   **Settings Component**: Provides the UI for users to interact with and modify tool configurations.
    *   [src/components/Settings.tsx](mdc:src/components/Settings.tsx)

## Features

*   **Categorization**: Tools are grouped into logical categories (e.g., AnthropicComputerUse, Desktop, Browser).
*   **Persistence**: User configurations are saved to disk and loaded on application startup.
*   **Required Tools**: Certain essential tools can be marked as "required" and cannot be disabled by the user, ensuring core functionality remains active.
*   **Granular Control**: Users can toggle individual tools or entire categories on/off.
*   **Real-time Updates**: Changes made in the settings UI are immediately reflected in the backend and vice-versa.
